id: pm-fqdmbf
title: "GH-803: hoist repeated linked-test execution context and honor lean output"
description: "pm test --run --json repeats a 16-field sandbox execution_context on every result even though the context is invocation-scoped; in the reported one-test case it consumes 727 of 1,301 bytes and grows redundantly with each linked test."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[8]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",context-management,gh-issue,linked-tests,output-contract,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-29T02:34:38.529Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T06:28:19.991Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-29T06:28:17.230Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-29T06:28:17.230Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Invocation-scoped execution context is emitted once rather than duplicated on every linked-test result, with no diagnostic information loss; Lean structured output omits non-actionable successful-run sandbox plumbing while failures retain enough provenance to diagnose context isolation; Default and full projections remain explicitly contracted and backward compatibility is handled through a documented schema/version strategy; CLI, SDK, MCP, JSON schemas, contracts, and documentation expose one consistent test-run output shape; Measured multi-test output proves a material byte and token reduction while focused and exact 100 percent coverage remain green"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Pay once for invocation provenance and reserve per-result output for result-specific evidence
value: Agents retain more context for actionable test failures and project decisions
impact: Removes multiplicative payload overhead from linked-test sweeps without discarding sandbox diagnostics
outcome: Structured linked-test output scales with useful results rather than repeated temporary-path plumbing
why_now: GH-803 measured execution_context at 56 percent of a passing one-test JSON response and identified per-result duplication that worsens with fleet sweeps
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
repro_steps: "Enable test-result-tracking in a fresh workspace, link multiple passing tests, run pm test --run --json, and compare repeated execution_context bytes with result-specific bytes."
resolution: "Real CLI test output hoists shared execution context, preserves mixed arrays, and removes only non-actionable successful streams in lean mode."
expected_result: "One invocation-level execution context plus compact result-specific records, with lean success output and diagnostic failure output."
actual_result: "Every result repeats the same 16-field sandbox context, including temporary absolute paths, regardless of status or lean intent."
affected_version: 2026.7.29
component: linked-test-output-contract
customer_impact: Fleet-wide linked-test sweeps spend most structured output on repeated sandbox plumbing that cannot change an agent decision.
