comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T02:34:38.529Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: all-status searches for execution_context, sandbox plumbing, lean output, and GH-778 found closed pm-oi4zs3 for caller echoes and inactive pagination metadata plus open pm-5t33or/pm-cxr0jb for general budget and intent projections. None owns invocation-level hoisting or status-aware linked-test provenance, so GH-803 is a distinct successor in that canonical lineage: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/803."
  "2026-07-29T05:55:21.096Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence: CLI linked-test output hoists identical invocation context once, retains heterogeneous per-row context, removes successful streams in lean JSON, and preserves failure diagnostics. Output unit coverage and exact token gates passed."
  "2026-07-29T06:26:33.005Z","harness:codex","PR #809 review evidence: real Commander command identity now reaches output formatting, so runtime pm test activates context hoisting; mixed run_results arrays remain byte-faithful. Post-review black-box CLI acceptance proved one shared context and lean rows without successful streams."
